"""Single-point mutants of experiments/exp_astro_clusterdep.py (the cluster-dependence study: diagnosis of the spent patches, the freeze, the held-out run, the verdicts, the report), for tools/mutants.py:

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_astro_clusterdep --tests tests/test_exp_astro_clusterdep.py --raw results/astro/clusterdep_raw.npz --md results/astro/clusterdep.md --out-env CLUSTERDEP_OUT \\
        --spec tools/mutants/wp_clusterdep_own.py --work <scratch dir> [--slot a --i0 0 --step 2]

A tuple is (id, what, old, new[, k]): `old` replaced by `new` at its k-th occurrence in experiments/exp_astro_clusterdep.py. The kill criterion is the tests file alone (planted worlds: no real patch is read; the
real raw is copied into the slot for the md column only). The functions mutated are those of this script: the module `astro_clusterdep.py` (the merge, the coherence table, the calibration) has its own spec
(`wp_clusterdep_lib_own.py`), the functions it imports (`exp_astro_m2`, `exp_astro_psf`, `exp_astro_cyclefix`, `exp_astro_fresh`, `astro_fresh`, `astro_common`) are covered by their own test files and specs.

Final result (three passes: the whole spec against the first tests file, then the survivors against the sharpened tests, 79 tests in all): 120 mutants, 118 killed, 2 survivors, both equivalent on every input:
  K01  `pkey` with the origin swapped: the key is only used to write and read the same arrays, so swapping the components of every key changes nothing a test or the report can see.
  C10  the `(D > 0)` in `f15`: `br` (a strictly brighter neighbour) is already False for the star itself, so the extra condition is redundant.
WORDING ROUND (after the referee report C+D: the failed registrations, the two scorings side by side, the seed sensitivity, the cluster-level permutation, the roles in the tally): Y01-Y32 added (88 tests in all). All 32 killed by the
tests file alone, run with `-k "registration or verdicts_subset or side_by_side or knife or loco_means or permutation or roundness or tally or heldout"` (the tests that read the new functions; the whole file takes a minute per mutant).
A first pass of the new tests has the planted-world pitfalls recorded in their docstrings (a planted patch whose scoring as it is has no matched star cannot fail its registration; gaps symmetric about their mean make a second
permutation exact).
A first pass left 20 survivors (covariate formulas, decomposition boundaries, freeze refusals, report columns, the planted world in which the repair changed nothing); each was killed by a test added for it.
"""
